1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
[Shoot] Given his personality,

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
it's safe to assume
that he's already been won over.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
I doubt he would knowingly sell me out,

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
[opening theme music playing]

5
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,000
[singer singing in English]

6
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:34,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

7
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
[narrator] There was a man
targeting Gon and Killua

8
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,000
and his name is Shoot McMahon.

9
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,000
[Killua grunts] No use.

10
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:36,000
The way we are now,
we don't stand a chance.

11
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,000
When I take my target down,
I'm always deliberate and thorough.

12
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,000
[boys grunting]

13
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,000
[Shoot] Go. This is it.

14
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,000
What's wrong?
It's the perfect opportunity.

15
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
I could easily just…

16
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,000
[grunts, shudders]

17
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,000
[straining] Go.

18
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Go!

19
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:46,000
[groaning]

20
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,000
[continues weeping]

21
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:12,000
[Gon] Hey, Killua.
Why wasn't Mr. Knuckle good enough?

22
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Wait. For what?

23
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,000
To get inside the NGL?

24
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,000
I mean, he's really strong.
I just don't get it.

25
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
I guess you're right.

26
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,000
It doesn't make any sense.

27
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:25,000
Physically he seems like
he'd be right on par with Kite.

28
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Yeah, but his personality…

29
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Why does that matter?

30
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:33,000
His philosophy isn't in line
with the mission's objective.

31
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,000
He's fragile.

32
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:38,000
And he gets attached to animals
way too easily.

33
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,000
[Gon] Yeah.

34
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,000
[imperceptible]

35
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,000
[Biscuit] They can maintain their Ren
for two hours

36
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,000
without even having to concentrate.

37
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:00,000
That's a good sign.

38
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,000
If they can do it for three hours,

39
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,000
I might let them fight
when they're fully rested.

40
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:17,000
I can only hope that
then they'll be able to realize

41
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,000
what they lack and what they need.

42
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
But that only gets them halfway.

43
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,000
If everything goes well,

44
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:27,000
it'll take them about ten days
to reach that point.

45
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:34,000
And that means they'll barely have
a day left before time is completely up.

46
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,000
I'm not convinced we can make it.

47
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,000
-[knife chopping]
-[Palm humming]

48
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:05,000
[Biscuit] If I want to save my own skin,
I should probably prepare an escape route.

49
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:11,000
-[Palm] Help yourself.
-[Gon and Killua] Thank you for the food!

50
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:26,000
[Palm] Not that.
We only have ten days left.

51
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:31,000
It looks to me like you're two-thirds
of the way through your training

52
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:33,000
which is meant to make you both
strong enough

53
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:37,000
to force Knuckle into using
his full power in battle.

54
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:41,000
[Biscuit] Uh-oh.
She knows exactly what's going on.

55
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:54,000
[Palm scoffs] But how can you be so sure?

56
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:10,000
You have no chance of beating Knuckle.
They didn't even give you enough time.

57
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:15,000
Lately, I find that I can calm myself
by staring at my knife,

58
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:20,000
and that can only mean I'm getting
dangerously close to losing it.

59
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:22,000
If you run away right now,

60
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:25,000
I probably won't hunt you down
and kill you.

61
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:41,000
Because you definitely can't win
as you are at the moment.

62
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:53,000
[sing-song]
I hereby swear that Killua and I

63
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:56,000
will take down Knuckle and Shoot
before the deadline comes.

64
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:02,000
I pinky-swear, so if I lie you can stick
a thousand needles right in my eye.

65
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Where I'm from, we do this next.

66
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:15,000
-[heart beats]
-[Palm gasps]

67
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,000
There. Now it's a real promise.

68
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:21,000
By the way, Miss Palm,
what's in the broth?

69
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:25,000
[Palm breathing heavily]
Oh, it's from poultry.

70
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:31,000
I guess not everyone can handle her,
but Gon's getting better.

71
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:37,000
but I suspect
she's actually the one handling him.

72
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:40,000
I just put a kunai chicken
on to simmer overnight,

73
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,000
-then set it aside for later.
-Wow.

74
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,000
Well, ten days left.

75
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,000
-[Gon] It's awesome!
-You say that like we're screwed!

76
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:05,000
[Baital] This is it.

77
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
Baital Squad here.
What's the update, Goran?

78
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,000
Goran, do you read me? Hello?

79
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:22,000
Damn it! Did they get him already?

80
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:27,000
Is there anyone
from Goran's squad out there?

81
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:48,000
[Baital huffs]
These signals are getting all mashed up.

82
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:50,000
They should've established
a contact network

83
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,000
in case the leader goes missing.

84
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:57,000
Baital Squad, find Goran's squadron
and rendezvous with them.

85
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Proceed in crane formation.

86
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,000
[grunting]

87
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,000
[grunts]

88
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,000
[Netero grunts]

89
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,000
So you're next, huh?

90
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,000
[Morel] You really think this is fair?

91
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,000
[Knov] What do you mean?

92
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:23,000
The Chairman is still much stronger
than we are.

93
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,000
And he seems rather excited.

94
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,000
[cell phone beeping]

95
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,000
[groans]

96
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Hey, speak of the devil, huh?

97
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:37,000
You can keep sending them my way.

98
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:40,000
I'm finally starting
to get my groove back.

99
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,000
That's pretty impressive, sir.

100
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,000
[chuckles softly]

101
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Then I think we can assume
that the King hasn't been born yet.

102
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,000
-[Morel] Roger that.
-[line disconnects]

103
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,000
He's old, but he's in top form.

104
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:11,000
-[Knov] Shall we go grab another squadron?
-Sure.

105
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Gaftz's and Baital's squads
haven't returned yet.

106
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:25,000
We're down to 14 squads.

107
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:27,000
Those damned humans.

108
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:31,000
How in the world are they managing
to whittle us down like this?

109
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,000
No clue.

110
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:38,000
All I know is that there are some humans
out there who are quite powerful.

111
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
[sighs]

112
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:43,000
We know very little about them,
far less than I'm comfortable with.

113
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:48,000
Their powers appear so varied
and seem much stronger than our own.

114
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,000
If we just had more time,

115
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Yes, I hope you're right.

116
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:07,000
[Queen laughing]

117
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,000
[liquid sloshes]

118
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:15,000
[gasps] Do you want to come out now?

119
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:16,000
[laughs]

120
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:19,000
Not yet.

121
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:22,000
It's still too early.

122
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,000
[Gon] Yeah. That seemed fast.

123
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:38,000
Then I suppose I'll give you a break,
take 30 minutes.

124
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:40,000
-Really?
-Aren't we supposed to fight Knuckle now?

125
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:44,000
I'll allow you two to go
once you're fully rested.

126
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,000
You can take him.

127
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,000
[both gasp]

128
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:50,000
The Chairman's deadline
is fast approaching.

129
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Just over a day left.

130
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:55,000
So this may be
your first and final chance.

131
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
[boys grunt]

132
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:14,000
[Palm humming]

133
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:21,000
[muttering]

134
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:29,000
[Biscuit] The problem now
is how to escape?

135
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Hmm?

136
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:47,000
[dogs snort]

137
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,000
You boys mean business tonight.

138
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:17,000
[violin music playing]

139
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,000
[violin music continues playing]

140
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Hmm.

141
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,000
[footsteps thudding]

142
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,000
Good morning, Youpi.

143
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:08,000
I'm getting real hungry.

144
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:21,000
What? Are you talking about Shoot?

145
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:22,000
Yeah.

146
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:24,000
Why do you want to know about that?

147
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:27,000
You're about to get the crap
knocked out of you, kid.

148
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,000
Because we need both of your tiles.

149
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,000
You're just messing with me, right?

150
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:35,000
If you can beat me,
I'll answer your question.

151
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:40,000
We might not get a chance then,
not if your laying unconscious.

152
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:41,000
[grunts]

153
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:47,000
You just went too far
with that little joke.

154
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,000
[yelling]

155
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:54,000
[grunting]

156
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,000
Here!

157
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,000
-[Gon grunts]
-Gon!

158
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:19,000
[Gon] That hit hard.
I could feel it through my whole body.

159
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:22,000
Without Ken, his next punch
will definitely knock me out.

160
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:28,000
Four or five more warm-up punches,
and I'll get serious.

161
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:31,000
So you better watch yourselves, boys.

162
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:35,000
'Cause I get warmed up pretty damn fast.

163
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,000
Shall we make our move now?

164
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,000
We can wait until they're ready.

165
00:18:57,000 --> 00:19:01,000
[Knov] Judging by the estimated number
of bodies currently stored in the nest,

166
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:04,000
they'll need to restock
in another week or so.

167
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:10,000
And whenever that happens,
I'd like to dispatch a few more squadrons.

168
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:13,000
[Netero] I leave that up to you.

169
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:14,000
[line disconnects]

170
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:23,000
We don't move from here
until we know how our pupils did.

171
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,000
Huh.

172
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:26,000
I think it's a waste of time.

173
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:29,000
Knuckle and Shoot can assist,

174
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:33,000
but the old man's kids
don't seem like they're all that reliable.

175
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:36,000
So we can't count on them in a battle.

176
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:39,000
The best we could hope for
is to use them as decoys.

177
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:59,000
I'll put down 100,000
on Knuckle and Shoot.

178
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:02,000
If neither of us wins,
the Chairman gets the money.

179
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,000
[Knov] Sure.

180
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:09,000
Then, I'll put…

181
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,000
one million on them.

182
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:18,000
Huh? There's no way in hell
they're gonna be ready by then.

183
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,000
What, are you trying
to throw all your money to the dogs?

184
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:24,000
The Chairman is a dog now?

185
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:28,000
[scoffs] I happen to love gambling.

186
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:31,000
And when it's a long shot, all the better.

187
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:35,000
[both grunting]

188
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:43,000
Behind you!

189
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:47,000
[gasps]

190
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:56,000
[grunts]

191
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,000
[Gon] This is supposed to be a warm up?

192
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:04,000
Damn, he's strong!

193
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:06,000
But why is Knuckle…

194
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:07,000
Could it be?

195
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:12,000
Come on, let me see that technique.
That "Show me rock" thing?

196
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:24,000
A small word of advice:

197
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:29,000
If you do try that attack,
then you're going down. [chuckles]

198
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:44,000
Your signature technique
currently has exactly two major flaws.

199
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:12,000
[closing theme music playing]

200
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:24,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

201
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,000
[upbeat music playing]

202
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:43,000
-And reassurance!
-[Biscuit] Oh, come on!

203
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:48,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
